Afterwards there is a translation from Spanish to English but the syntax doesn't work well.  Best to just stumble through the Spanish if you don't speak it.
 
TIP:  Try to play the full (E7) chord as indicated to get that treble <d> note.  It's easy as it'll always follow an (E) so just add your pinky to the second string/3rd fret.

TIP:  At the end, <raking> means to strum back and forth rapidly in a sawing motion.
   

